"{\"url\":\"https://registry.isometric.com/project/prj_1JQEW95GA1S0D2FD\",\"title\":\"Treehouse Plant 1 — Isometric\",\"head\":[\"UNDER VALIDATION\",\"BICRS\",\"Treehouse Plant 1\",\"Sitos Group\",\"->\",\"PROJECT DETAILS\",\"Expected first certificates\",\"2026\",\"Project code\",\"QVP9\",\"Crediting period\",\"01 Apr 2026 to 01 Apr 2031\"],\"issued_header\":null,\"buffer_header\":null,\"crediting\":null,\"verifier\":null,\"code\":\"QVP9\",\"approval\":\"Expected 2026\",\"protocol_current\":\"Biochar Production and Storage v1.3\",\"protocol_baseline\":null,\"cert_issued\":null,\"cert_retired\":null,\"cert_buffer\":null,\"reversal\":null,\"showing\":[\"Showing 2 of 2\"],\"tables\":[{\"heads\":[\"Submission date\",\"Title\",\"Download\"],\"rows\":[[\"21 Sep 2025\",\"Public Comment Summary\",\"PDF | ->\"],[\"17 Aug 2025\",\"PDD\",\"PDF | ->\"]]}],\"links\":[{\"h\":\"https://sitos.earth\",\"t\":\"Sitos Group\"},{\"h\":\"/protocol/biochar/1.3\",\"t\":\"Biochar Production and Storage v1.3\"},{\"h\":\"/supplier/spl_1JPQD8EW91S0KESK\",\"t\":\"Learn more\"},{\"h\":\"https://registry.isometric.com/standard#validation-and-verification-process\",\"t\":\"Isometric Standard\"},{\"h\":\"https://storage.googleapis.com/isometric--production--eu--public-documents/spl_1JPQD8EW91S0KESK/prj_1JQEW95GA1S0D2FD/pjd_1K5RA59NN1S01PDW/public_comment_summary.pdf\",\"t\":\"PDF | ->\"},{\"h\":\"https://storage.googleapis.com/isometric--production--eu--public-documents/spl_1JPQD8EW91S0KESK/prj_1JQEW95GA1S0D2FD/pjd_1K4B7E7A21S0373Y/pdd.pdf\",\"t\":\"PDF | ->\"}],\"text\":\"UNDER VALIDATION\\nBICRS\\nTreehouse Plant 1\\nSitos Group\\n->\\nPROJECT DETAILS\\nExpected first certificates\\n2026\\nProject code\\nQVP9\\nCrediting period\\n01 Apr 2026 to 01 Apr 2031\\nPROTOCOL DETAILS\\nCurrent protocol version\\nBiochar Production and Storage v1.3\\nSummary\\n\\nSitos Treehouse Plant 1, LLC transforms almond shell into highly durable biochar—made by growers, used by growers—to store carbon, enrich soils, and build a more regenerative future.\\n\\nDelano, CA\\nHow carbon is being removed\\n\\nBiomass Carbon Removal and Storage (BiCRS) involves storing the carbon contained in waste biomass—organic material from living or recently living organisms. BiCRS works by halting or slowing the decomposition of biomass, enabling the carbon it contains to be stored long-term. This can be achieved by converting biomass into materials that decompose more slowly—such as biochar or bio-oil—or by storing it in environments where decomposition is slowed. For BiCRS to count as carbon removal, the biomass must be replenished to ensure additional carbon dioxide is drawn from the atmosphere.\\n\\nLearn more\\nProject timeline\\nCompleted 26 Aug 2025\\nPublic comment period\\nCompleted 2026\\nInitial documentation submission\\nCompleted 2026\\nAudit kick-off\\nExpected 2026\\nIN PROGRESS\\nSite visit\\n\\nIsometric’s qualified VVB conducts a site visit, comparing the project facility against the documentation provided. The required cadence for site visits is defined in the Isometric Standard.\\n\\nExpected 2026\\nApproval date\\nExpected 2026\\nInitial credit issuance\\nProject documentation\\nSubmission date\\tTitle\\tDownload\\n21 Sep 2025\\tPublic Comment Summary\\tPDF\\n->\\n\\n17 Aug 2025\\tPDD\\tPDF\\n->\\nShowing 2 of 2\\nPrevious\\nNext\"}"